    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers heavily on exploiting favorable matchups against higher xERA starters, led by the day's highest-scored asset, **Corbin Carroll** (87.14). **Corbin Carroll** is in a prime position to leverage his elite speed against Sugano, who offers an advantageous 5.02 xERA, allowing **Corbin Carroll** to maximize his stolen base potential in a favorable park environment. **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Gabriel Moreno** (71.10) follow closely as primary targets, both benefiting from significantly elevated SP Skill modifiers and park factors that lift them well into our \"Strong\" tier. **Brice Turang** (67.46) also remains a core staple; his leadoff role against the 4.43 xERA of Buehler gives him a distinct efficiency advantage for building R/SB accumulation early.\n\nWhile we are leaning into high-upside offensive environments, we are exercising caution with players facing tougher arms. **Josh Naylor** (48.81) and **Austin Riley** (47.47) are seeing suppressed scores due to negative SP Skill adjustments when facing Weathers and McLean, respectively. Similarly, **Cole Young** (45.30) is being started despite a marginal score, as his utility in the stolen base category necessitates inclusion, even if the matchup against Weathers is suboptimal. The most difficult decision today involved the benching of **Jose Caballero** (43.67); while he offers a high base projection, his batting order position (#8) and a negative platoon split against Woo forced the optimizer to favor the more consistent output of **Max Muncy** (61.22) and **Henry Bolte** (59.91) to maintain our ceiling.\n\nA critical reminder for today\u2019s slate: all positions are currently utilizing \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Should **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, or **Brice Turang** find themselves dropped in the order upon official confirmation, we may need to re-evaluate their efficiency scores. We remain without the services of **James Wood**, who continues to hold a 0.00 score due to his status on the IL. With **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** all currently sidelined or off the active card, we are relying heavily on the current depth chart to sustain our Roto momentum. Monitor the weather and lineup changes closely, as any late-breaking wind shifts could further impact the projected output for **Isaac Paredes**.",
